WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:06.749
Hey team it’s Charlie and since I already
posted a non-spoilery review of Gotham this

00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:09.429
is going to be a top 10 video that will be
a lot more specific.

00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:15.000
I saw on twitter that most of you guys were
divided.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.710
In terms of quality I’ll just say that the
pilot and the regular series usually look

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.360
very different.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.180
And when you consider a show like Agents of
SHIELD.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.510
Sometimes it can take a half a season for
it to find it’s legs.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.270
So if you had any issues with the premiere,
just stay with it.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.530
Fox already ordered 16 episodes, that’s
what season 1 will be 16 episodes.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.370
They’ve only shot some of those, so they
will be able to address feedback.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:43.250
I wish I’d said all that at the beginning
of SHIELD season 1 last year.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.260
But Gotham top 10 moments from the premiere.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.690
I should call this top 10 Batman easter eggs.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.879
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:52.679
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go

00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:54.780
Number 10 - Selina Kyle’s introduction

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.949
This really reminded me of the beginning of
Tim Burton’s Batman, with the way it opened

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:01.199
with the mugging.

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:05.160
It was michael keaton on the rooftop that
time but essentially it opens with a crime

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.330
being committed.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.060
And I like that they’re tying her to the
scene of the Wayne Murder.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.120
There are so many different batman titles
in the comics, I can’t remember if there

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.020
was ever a version of the origin story where
Selina Kyle was present at their murder, so

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.150
I’ll say this is something new to the show.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.240
It’s just a way to bind their characters
across time and space.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.950
I’ll bet that both Selina’s story and
Bruce’s story will be good mirrors of each

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.950
other.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:35.350
We’ll actually be able to test that theory
next week as Episode 2 will focus mostly on

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.350
her character.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.350
Number 9 - The Murder of course

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:42.780
This scene has been done in every single version
of every batman story since the dawn of time.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.110
The thing that’s different each time is
what people use it for in the story.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:50.350
In Gotham, the murder is going to be the macguffin
of season 1.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.610
Or finding the identity of the murderer.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:56.500
Because apparently even the most powerful
mob boss in the city has no idea who ordered

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.500
the hit.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.630
In case you missed it, Falcone is the boss
of bosses in Gotham, you could call him the

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:03.960
big bad but he’s morally gray.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.150
Not a straight up psychopath.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:09.219
Jada Pinkett Smith’s character is also a
mob boss, but answers to him.

00:02:09.219 --> 00:02:12.050
None of them seem to have a clue who ordered
the Wayne’s murder.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:16.670
It’s a little too soon to guess which villain
did it but with the way things come full circle

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.439
in most big murder mysteries, I’m guessing
Bullock or Barbara Kean’s father or someone

00:02:21.439 --> 00:02:23.870
close to Gordon had something to do with it.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:29.519
I’ll talk more about the mystery as we get
on through several episodes and learn more.

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:32.730
Number 8 - Bullock with the Paper

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.380
This is also a callback to Burton’s first
Batman movie when Vicki Vale is talking to

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:41.049
Alexander Knox and he makes the comment about
giant flying bats and the crime wave of the

00:02:41.049 --> 00:02:42.349
century.

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:46.439
As dark as Bullock got in the episode, I like
to think that Donal Logue got a good laugh

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:48.470
when he was doing this.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:52.349
His Bullock isn’t quite as angry as the
older version we see in the Animated Series.

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:58.060
I’m interested to learn more about how he’s
connected to the big players in the city.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:02.450
I’d guess he’s directly on Falcone’s
payroll but isn’t out to hurt people.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.830
He’s not an evil character.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:09.269
Hopefully what we’ll see is some episodes
told from Bullock’s perspective this season

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:11.950
that explain how he got to where he is.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.439
Number 7 - Meet the Penguin

00:03:13.439 --> 00:03:18.161
He’s one of the first batman villains we
see and I believe he’s supposed to be in

00:03:18.161 --> 00:03:19.290
his early twenties.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.859
Like 10 years older than bruce wayne.

00:03:21.859 --> 00:03:31.040
This whole episode was mostly dedicated to
him despite them cramming in so many other

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.439
characters.

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:38.329
His mother is going to be played by Carol
Kane, this is an actual image of her.

00:03:38.329 --> 00:03:41.889
You would probably turn into a supervillain
too if you grew up in a home like that.

00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:44.650
She has this amazing Grey Gardens look about
her.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:04:04.040
I liked that later, even when Oswald was staring
murder in the face, he got really pissed when

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.260
Mooney called him Penguin.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.420
He even limped penguin style when he was on
the pier with Gordon.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.219
Yes he was told to never come back, but of
course he’s coming back.

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.029
I’m looking forward to more Gordon Penguin
scenes.

00:04:15.029 --> 00:04:19.169
He spared his life so I’m interested to
see how Oswald returns the favor.

00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:24.289
The Penguin in the canon has had periods when
he tried to go legit.

00:04:24.289 --> 00:04:28.340
He’s one of those batman villains like the
Riddler, they don’t want to hurt people

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:30.770
or cause chaos just for the sake of chaos.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.050
They just want to build something of their
own.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.959
The reason they’re called batman villains
is because of what they do to get there, and

00:04:35.959 --> 00:04:38.490
when push comes to shove they start endangering
people's lives.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.300
Number 6 - Enter the Riddler

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.660
Edward Nygma is working in the police department
so we’ll get a lot more of him soon.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:49.280
In the canon as the riddler he’s worked
with the police before.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.389
He’s helped them solve cases in exchange
for money and public service he’s been ordered

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:54.389
to serve from past crimes.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:55.389
Here on the show as far as we know that’s
all ahead of him.

00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:58.270
I’m interested to see if he’s already
committing crimes or if we’ll get to see

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:06.130
him have a mental breakdown and just start
going nuts on the city.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:11.440
It seems like it would be too fun for them
to not tell that story.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:15.470
And since Gotham looks like it’s inspired
by the Tim Burton Batman, I’m wondering

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:20.699
if we’ll get a Michelle Pfiefer Catwoman
transformation scene.

00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:24.780
When you go back and re-watch scenes like
that you have to admire the attention to style

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:31.460
and TV is a place where they can have more
fun like that.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:37.580
Plus the Riddler has always been one of the
wackier batman villains, so I think a big

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.479
Nygma goes crazy scene would totally work
with the character.

00:05:40.479 --> 00:05:44.100
Number 5 - Meet Poison Ivy who lives at fourth
and Grundy

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.949
This is really like two things, so I’ll
do Grundy first.

00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:52.690
Arrow did Solomon Grundy in season 2 with
the whole Mirakuru army of blood storyline,

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:53.940
he didn’t die.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.930
Because Grundy can’t die, but on Gotham
it’s just an easter egg.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:58.930
Arrow does the same thing with street names
and signs.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:01.479
I don’t think Gotham will bring Grundy on
the show.

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:04.949
Ivy Pepper is a bit of a mystery on the show
right now.

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:08.939
Since she’s such a small character at this
point I don’t think we’ll see much from

00:06:08.939 --> 00:06:09.939
her right away.

00:06:09.939 --> 00:06:14.720
They might tie her to Selina Kyle’s character
in the way Harley Quinzel and Poison Ivy spent

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.689
a lot of time together in the comics and the
animated series.

00:06:17.689 --> 00:06:21.889
Since Gotham is just doing origin stories
I don’t expect to see any crazy Poison Ivy

00:06:21.889 --> 00:06:25.720
powers but hopefully they’ll let her have
some fun with Catwoman.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:33.409
Number 4 - Meet Barbara Kean fiancee of Gordon
and Former Lover of Montoya

00:06:33.409 --> 00:06:36.450
In the canon her character is always talked
about in past tense.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:40.100
She and Gordon are usually divorced by the
time he becomes commissioner gordon.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:46.940
Montoya talked about her past which was of
course a reference to their previous relationship.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.199
Montoya is a lesbian character in the canon.

00:06:49.199 --> 00:06:56.129
She also becomes The Question, so I felt like
when she was talking to Barbara she was also

00:06:56.129 --> 00:06:59.569
referring to some non-sexual extra curricular
activities.

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:03.940
I wondered for a brief minute if they were
going to turn Barbara Kean into Kathy Kane,

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:04.940
the Batwoman character from the comics.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:09.110
She was also a wealthy heiress just like Barbara
Kean is on the show and she’s a lesbian.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:13.439
I just felt like for a minute the show wanted
us to make that association with batwoman

00:07:13.439 --> 00:07:17.800
in the comics and this person on the show,
even if they’re not going in that direction.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.930
The show has cast Betty Kane, the original
Bat Girl in the comics.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.919
That’s going to be Sarah Paxton.

00:07:21.919 --> 00:07:23.909
No word on which episode she’ll appear in.

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:30.710
But I think it’s more likely they’ll do
batgirl than batwoman.

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.319
Or they could do both.

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:47.340
I totally dig the idea that all the vigilantes
in the city are hardcore females.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.979
Number 3 - Meet Carmine Falcone, Gotham’s
Boss of Bosses

00:07:50.979 --> 00:07:52.780
This character also appeared in Batman Begins.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.219
He was played by Tom Wilkinson.

00:07:55.219 --> 00:08:05.889
In the canon he was created to be like a Michael
Corleone figure from the Godfather.

00:08:05.889 --> 00:08:13.569
His father was also a mob boss, Thomas Wayne
saved his life and as a result Carmine told

00:08:13.569 --> 00:08:16.509
Bruce that he could always ask him a favor
if he needed it.

00:08:16.509 --> 00:08:19.009
They followed up on this during Batman Year
One.

00:08:19.009 --> 00:08:21.569
But here’s where it gets really interesting.

00:08:21.569 --> 00:08:24.719
In the comics Falcone is Selina Kyle’s father.

00:08:24.719 --> 00:08:29.229
It’s unclear if the show is going to deal
with this but I think it would be an interesting

00:08:29.229 --> 00:08:34.919
way to create more bonds between all the characters.

00:08:34.919 --> 00:08:41.890
Falcone on the show is slowly losing control
of the city, so we might meet some of the

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.589
contenders for the throne of Gotham soon.

00:08:44.589 --> 00:08:48.160
Number 2 - Gotham Central and all the big
characters we haven’t seen yet

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:57.560
THere’s a lot of Police characters from
the comics we haven’t seen yet that I expect

00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.130
to see eventually and add to that district
attorney Harvey Dent.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:02.380
Two face will be on the show eventually.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:06.700
They pretty much have their pick of the litter
when it comes to Gotham-centric batman characters.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:09.670
With one exception.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:18.610
and my Number 1 moment of course the Comedian.

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:21.890
No it was not the joker.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:26.220
What they teased this summer was that they’re
going to have a string of comedians come through

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:31.230
the club, like each time we see one, it will
be a different person.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:36.350
Fish Mooney auditioning comedians for her
club is going to be like the show auditioning

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:38.120
people for The Joker.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:42.320
You could also say that naming Jada Pinkett
Smith Fish Mooney is a subtle reference to

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:43.540
the joker’s Laughing Fish.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:47.880
That was an episode of the animated series
where the joker poisons the fish supply with

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:50.500
his neuro toxin.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.690
Her character isn’t someone from the comics,
there is no Fish Mooney reference I could

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.710
find.

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:59.740
I’m not expecting to see a Joker character
ever on the show, but I am expecting to see

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.000
references to him.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.390
And also, for people asking.

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:03.390
Since Arrow is doing Ra’s Al Ghul Gotham
will not.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.580
None of the shows are going to do the same
people at the same time.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.580
There’s no way DC Comics would allow that
kind of mass confusion.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.570
But let me know what your favorite moment
was and if you spotted any comic book references

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.440
in the episode just write them in the comics.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:15.930
I’ll be doing weekly Gotham videos so if
you like talking about Batman please subscribe

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.060
and join the team.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.420
We meet every monday night.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:22.320
Tomorrow is agents of shield season 2 episode
1, I’ll also be doing that every week.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:28.300
In related news a new walking dead trailer
just dropped, so that will be my next video.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.920
I’ll post that tomorrow morning.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:35.529
Right now click here for my non-spoilery review.

00:10:35.529 --> 00:10:40.089
I go into greater detail about what I thought
of the episode and click here for my agents

00:10:40.089 --> 00:10:41.640
of SHIELD season 2 preview.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.850
Thanks for watching, now everybody high five
and we’ll meet back up tomorrow.

